{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Adjust the \u00a310 Christmas \"Bonus\" for the needy to reflect 55 years of Inflation",
        "additional_details": "The winter months can see living costs rise (heating bills, Christmas gifts for family, extra food costs etc). We feel to issue \u00a310 to the people in society who have done their bit and/or can no longer work to raise income, and call it a \"Bonus\" is quite frankly insulting. In 1972, \u00a310 was a massive uplift to the poor, yet the amount has never been adjusted to reflect 55 years of inflation. Today, \u00a310 won't even pay for a family Christmas pudding, a decent box of crackers or a round of drinks.",
        "background": "In 1972, the government introduced a \u00a310 Christmas \"Bonus\" for Pensioners, Ex-Servicemen and the Disabled - people in society who need extra help during winter. 55 years ago, it would have been a massive uplift (approximately \u00a3180 back then adjusted for inflation). We want to address this issue.",
